#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:1
msgid ""
"**Warning**   \n"
"This program is [**experimental**](../../development/experimental-"
"features.md#xp-feature-nix-command) and its interface is subject to change."
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:6
msgid "Name"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:8
msgid ""
"`nix flake prefetch` - download the source tree denoted by a flake reference "
"into the Nix store"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:10
msgid "Synopsis"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:12
msgid "`nix flake prefetch` \\[_option_...\\] _flake-url_"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:14
msgid "Examples"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:16
msgid "Download a tarball and unpack it:"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:18
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix flake prefetch https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v5.x/"
"linux-5.10.5.tar.xz --out-link ./result\n"
"Downloaded 'https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v5.x/linux-5.10.5.tar.xz?"
"narHash=sha256-3XYHZANT6AFBV0BqegkAZHbba6oeDkIUCDwbATLMhAY='\n"
"to '/nix/store/sl5vvk8mb4ma1sjyy03kwpvkz50hd22d-source' (hash\n"
"'sha256-3XYHZANT6AFBV0BqegkAZHbba6oeDkIUCDwbATLMhAY=').\n"
"\n"
"# cat ./result/README\n"
"Linux kernel\n"
"…\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:29
msgid "Download the `dwarffs` flake (looked up in the flake registry):"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:31
msgid ""
"```console\n"
"# nix flake prefetch dwarffs --json\n"
"{\"hash\":\"sha256-VHg3MYVgQ12LeRSU2PSoDeKlSPD8PYYEFxxwkVVDRd0=\"\n"
",\"storePath\":\"/nix/store/l06r23gw4psl1f547il2hbnwnxaplbaz-source\"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:37
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: source/command-ref/new-cli/nix3-flake-prefetch.md:39
msgid ""
"This command downloads the source tree denoted by flake reference _flake-"
"url_. Note that this does not need to be a flake (i.e. it does not have to "
"contain a `flake.nix` file)."
msgstr ""

